{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwYS1k39NcKDALTuV8Ma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its status is still \"pending\", because I didn't wait for the first run. I also didn't open the dashboard to check how the panels render.\n\n**What the data holds:** the logs index has about 14,000 web requests. The fields cover the client IP, geo source and destination, the file extension, the response code, bytes transferred and the machine's OS and RAM. `response` is a string field, and the codes present are 200 (12,832), 404 (801) and 503 (441).\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-6c5a6ee7 Web logs overview\" (id `eff-6c5a6ee7-web-logs-overview-ffdaa8439914`) has four panels over the last 7 days:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Total bytes by extension\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-6c5a6ee7 5xx spike\" (id `30a8748b-f87d-4c0e-b4bc-8f8e124bebdc`) is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It counts documents where `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" over the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10.\n\nThe sample data is static, so the rule will only fire if its timestamps fall inside a rolling 5-minute window. I didn't add any notification action, so a firing would only show up in the rule's own status."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":20963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":506},"output_tokens":458,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"76ae28f6-58da-4f34-8d33-5f48b81fd3b0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:19:44.189Z","request_id":"req_011CfwYS1HkArjsdWxh